==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Cat O'Lantern''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Harbinger Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
Very similar to [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]] in terms of usage. Cheap and expendable, it can be summoned en masse to take hits in place of other, more important units. This meatshield role is quite valuable, if not for the wide selection of cats able to perform this role, usually with a lower cost. Pumpcat, however, can be used in [[Restriction Stage]]s that allow [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cats]] (such as [[Wrath of D-Cyclone (Insane)|Wrath of D-Cyclone]]), where there is considerably less competition. Even then, Pumpcat is still not one of the best options due to its slightly higher cost.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Cat O'Lantern is unreliable as an [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|anti-Dark Cat]]. Not only does it have about 6 seconds between attacks and freeze for only 2~2.4 seconds, its freeze chance is low as well, which means a Cat O'Lantern takes over 30 seconds just for one freeze. Its recharge time somewhat makes up for this by allowing you to create a stack, but then there comes another issue: single-target attacks. Most Dark enemies come in groups, so on top of only freezing every once in a blue moon, only one enemy will be frozen at a time. Since Dark enemies also tend to have many knockbacks, it might miss and be even less reliable. The icing on the cake is that most Dark enemies from [[Legend Stages]] are strong enough to kill even a level 50 Cat O'Lantern in one or two hits, which will destroy your entire stack in seconds.

Cat O'Lantern's only possible use is against [[Razorback]], if you do not have [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] or [[Oda Nobunaga (Uber Rare Cat)|Oda Nobunaga]]. For the reasons stated above, it alone will rarely be enough; it has to be supported by other crowd-controllers such as [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Cat Eastwood]] and [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Holy Valkyrie Cat]]. If you have Bombercat, you can and should use him as a permanent replacement for Cat O'Lantern.

As ineffective as Cat O'Lantern is in [[Battle|battle]], it's worth getting just for the [[Pumpkinpants (Combo)|Pumpkinpants]] Combo, which can be combined with [[Gross!!! (Combo)|Gross!!!]] to greatly enhance the performance of units relying on freeze effects.

==='''True Form'''===
Even with Behemoth Slayer and Strong abilities, Harbinger Cat remains far too weak to be relevant. Most Dark enemies, which boast extreme DPS and numbers, can and will cut through it in seconds. On top of that, much more reliable options exist for this niche. Any niche it could have as an anti-Dark meatshield is already covered by [[Ancient Egg: N103 (Rare Cat)|Gas Mask Cat]], [[Nono (Rare Cat)|Nono]] and [[Li'l Gau (Rare Cat)|Li'l Gau]], while the likes of [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] and [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Assassin BearCat]] outclass it in the attack department. Also counterintuitively, [[Ragin' Gory]], [[Casaurian Darkjo]] and [[Crocodylidae Kurocroc]], the only Dark [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoths]], are all immune to freeze, giving this unit an even more ill-suited matchup.

The only reason you would ever get its True Form is for [[Go to Hell! (Combo)|Go to Hell!]] Combo which greatly help Weaken debuffers, but is also currently the only way for [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Headmaster Cat Jobs]] to reach 100% Weaken uptime against Traitless, Relic and Aku enemies if you added another Weaken Combo.

Even then, you likely won't get to use the Combo as you would need to complete Stories of Legends, obtain Elder Catfruit, [[WAVE BUSTERS (Gacha Event)|Wave Busters]] exclusive [[Hell Warden Emma (Uber Rare Cat)|unit]] and alot Behemoth Stones just to use it. So for most player, this True Form will likely remain in hell for who know how long.

